## No Unity MCP here — park editor work, do not fake it

Cursor cannot compile this project, enter Play mode, author scene objects, or capture the Game view. Most `done-when` criteria in `BACKLOG.md` require exactly that.

So: implement the code, re-read every changed file for syntax and API errors, then mark the task **`[?] needs Unity pass — <what specifically>`** instead of `[x]`, and say so in the commit message. Every task carries a `Unity:` field describing what the editor is needed for.

The `/unity-pass` command (Claude Code, which has Unity MCP) sweeps those `[?]` items later, does the editor-side work, and resolves each to `[x]` or a filed bug. Never mark a task `[x]` on the strength of reading the code — unverified is fine, falsely verified is not.

## Verified pitfalls (full text in AGENTS.md — read before FX/visual/view-mode work)

1. `SectorRuntime` is ONE shared GameObject; most FX systems are components on it, and props/dressing
   are its children. Inside such a component, `gameObject.AddComponent`, `GetComponentsInChildren<Renderer>`,
   `DontDestroyOnLoad(gameObject)` and reparenting `transform` all hit the entire runtime subtree. Put
   per-feature geometry / lights / visibility toggles on a dedicated child object, never on the runtime.
2. A scalar metric (mean luma, bounds gap, collision count) cannot tell "broken" from "measured wrong."
   Verify visuals by rendering the camera to an image and looking at it, from a real gameplay viewpoint.
3. State set this frame (LateUpdate writes, ViewMode.OnChanged reactions, gravity) is not readable the
   same frame. Change in one step, read in the next after frames advance.

